<title>UK: GEC,Thomson-CSF sign infra-red deal.</title>
<headline>GEC,Thomson-CSF sign infra-red deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The General Electric Co's defence firm GEC-Marconi said on Thursday it has agreed with French group Thomson-CSF to cooperate in the development and production of infra-red seekers for guided missiles.</p>
<p>&quot;This cooperation brings together the established expertise of two leading UK and French companies to provide Europe with a strong competitive capability to win world markets,&quot; GEC said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the deal was aimed initially at work on the seekers for the Storm Shadow/SCALP conventionally-armed cruise missiles being developed for the French and British air forces.</p>
<p>GEC and the soon-to-be privatised French defence electronics group are working on the missiles as sub-contractors to the Matra BAe Dynamics missiles joint venture owned by Lagardere and British Aerospace.</p>
<p>-- Greg Mahlich, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
